It does. It does not use SDRAM DIMMs if that is what you mean.
But EDO/FP based DIMMs are also an industry standard.

> My current guess is that it uses 5v edo/fp dimms.
> ( based on the difference in the notches, and the
> fact that 5v only exists for fp/edo ).

I just checked the User Information manual and that says
you need sets of 4 DIMMs.

> Though no-one really seems to know :(.
> 
> If someone knows the memory type then I'd like
> to know because it would save me loads of time
> chasing down the original stuff.

Well, they definitely use buffered DIMMs, I have some sitting
here on my desk (my AS500 was borrowed by a friend).

In case you want to research if they are EDO or FPM, the chips on the
DIMMs are SEC KM44C4000AS-6

Given that the AS600 uses FPM (to the best of my knowledge) I guess 
AS500 has FPM as well (but I could be wrong).

